# EXAMPLE settings for robodr-uplink.service (connected sites: the unit or
# sensor box sends agentd's spool to the SOC's AutoSecOps ingest API).
# Install as /etc/robodr/uplink.env, mode 0640 root:robodr:
#   install -m 0640 -o root -g robodr uplink.env.example /etc/robodr/uplink.env
# The unit refuses to start without this file (AssertPathExists=), needs
#   /etc/robodr/keys/uplink.key   the sender key (robodr-blackbox keygen,
#                                 0600 root:root; register uplink.key.pub in
#                                 AutoSecOps as this robot's `uplink` key)
#   /etc/robodr/uplink-ca.pem     the SOC's CA certificate(s) (PEM)
# and can reach no address until the 50-soc.conf drop-in lists the SOC.

# Required: the AutoSecOps API root; /robot-edr/v2/ingest is appended.
# https only (plain http:// is refused except to a loopback IP literal).
# The host must be the name the server certificate is issued for; map it
# in /etc/hosts (the unit cannot reach a DNS server unless the drop-in
# allows one). Documentation placeholder: replace it. TUNE.
ROBODR_UPLINK_URL=https://soc.example.org/api

# Optional extra flags (split on white space), see robodr-uplink(1), e.g.
# the server key pin (SHA-256 of its DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo, 64 hex; one
# --spki-sha256 per accepted key during a rotation):
#   --spki-sha256 <64 hex> --interval-ms 2000 --max-lines 500
ROBODR_UPLINK_ARGS=
